Use the raphael panel height in the touch offset so touch and display agree.

0061 presents the display as the iPhone X panel: 1125x2436 logical, with
the physical panel centred inside it.  SweetFramebuffer knows the real
panel size -- it reads it from the device tree -- and computes

    fOffX = (fLogicalW - fWidth) / 2;
    fOffY = (fLogicalH - fHeight) / 2;

On the raphael panel (1080x2340) that is (22, 48).

SweetHID cannot know the panel size, so 0061 hard coded the 2400 of the
guacamole panel:

    fLogicalW = native ? 1080 : 1125;
    fLogicalH = native ? 2400 : 2436;
    fOffX = (fLogicalW - 1080) / 2;
    fOffY = (fLogicalH - 2400) / 2;

which gives (22, 18).  The digitizer and the framebuffer therefore
disagree by 30 logical pixels in Y: every touch lands 30 points above the
finger, and the swipe up from the bottom edge never reaches the home
indicator, so the screen cannot be unlocked.

The fix is to use the raphael panel height 2340 in both places where
0061 mentions 2400.  The 1080 of the width is correct on raphael as
well and stays untouched.

  * native mode presents the real panel, so its logical height is the
    panel height: 2400 -> 2340.
  * the offset is the distance between the logical and the native size,
    so the subtraction changes from 2400 to 2340: (2436 - 2340) / 2 = 48,
    which is exactly what SweetFramebuffer computes.

The digitizer reports the raw panel coordinates (0060 hands them over
without any scaling), so the raw y range is 0..2339 on raphael and the
2340 is exactly the right divisor.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
@@ -426,9 +426,9 @@
 	int native = 0;
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_native", &native, sizeof(native));
 	fLogicalW = native ? 1080 : 1125;
-	fLogicalH = native ? 2400 : 2436;
+	fLogicalH = native ? 2340 : 2436;
 	fOffX = (fLogicalW - 1080) / 2;
-	fOffY = (fLogicalH - 2400) / 2;
+	fOffY = (fLogicalH - 2340) / 2;
 	/* The digitizer covers the main display (backboardd maps it 1:1). */
 	setProperty("DisplayIntegrated", kOSBooleanTrue);
 	setProperty("SurfaceWidth", (unsigned long long)(68 << 16), 32);	/* mm, 16.16 */
